# 5. MOTION DESIGN AND INTERACTIONS

Use GSAP and GSAP ScrollTrigger.

Animation level: RICH.

Animations must feel premium, smooth and purposeful.

## 5.1 Initial page load

- Subtle hero entrance.
- Headline reveals.
- Images fade and slide into position.
- Staggered timing.
- Avoid long loading animations.

The visitor must see the main content immediately.

## 5.2 Mouse-responsive hero

Implement:
- Mouse position tracking.
- Independent movement of image layers.
- Different movement strengths.
- Smooth easing.
- Return-to-position animation.

Use requestAnimationFrame or an equivalent efficient approach.

The effect must be disabled on touch devices.

## 5.3 Scroll-triggered animations

Use ScrollTrigger for:
- Headline reveals.
- Image masks.
- Staggered content entrances.
- Statistic count-up.
- Subtle parallax.
- Section transitions.

Avoid animating every single element.

Animations must not interfere with normal scrolling.

## 5.4 Project hover effects

When hovering over a project:
- Change the background to its assigned accent color.
- Slightly scale the image.
- Reveal supporting text or metadata.
- Smoothly transition back on mouse leave.

Use CSS custom properties for per-project colors.

## 5.5 Buttons and links

Implement:
- Subtle hover transitions.
- Smooth arrow movement.
- Clear active states.
- Accessible focus states.

## 5.6 Performance

- Avoid unnecessary event listeners.
- Avoid expensive DOM operations.
- Use transform and opacity where possible.
- Avoid excessive blur and filter effects.
- Use passive listeners when appropriate.
- Use IntersectionObserver where suitable.
- Clean up GSAP animations and listeners when necessary.

## 5.7 Accessibility

Respect:

`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`

When enabled:
- Disable parallax.
- Disable nonessential animated transitions.
- Display content immediately.
- Keep all functionality available.

